# What LibHac (MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Alex Barney), as Ryubing maintains it, reads that the pinned hactool cannot:
# - sparse sections (NcaSparseInfo, SparseStorage): a base whose update replaces part of it keeps only the rest;
# - compressed sections (NcaCompressionInfo, CompressedStorage): RomFS blocks in LZ4 or as zeros, hashed as stored;
# - bucket trees of any size (BucketTree): past 2046 entry sets a table has L2 nodes, which hactool's BKTR reader
#   did not know, and an update's tables may be followed by gaps and integrity metadata, which it refused;
# - AesCtrEx runs left unencrypted (AesCtrCounterExtendedStorage), and updates with no AesCtrEx entries (Ryubing);
# - gamecard dumps that start with the card's 0x1000-byte key area (XciHeader).
# storage.c holds the ported storages. nca.c reads every section through a chain of them, built as LibHac's Nca builds
# it (sparse, decryption, indirect, decompression past the hash layers), in place of its own CTR, XTS and BKTR
# seeking, including the plaintext BKTR reads of hactool-decrypted.patch. Encryption types 5 and 6 (skip layer hash)
# and the SHA3 hash types, which LibHac names but does not read, are refused with a message.
#
# It applies after hactool-decrypted.patch and hactool-openssl.patch (cmake/hactool.cmake). To change it, edit copies
# of the files those two patches make, rebuild the hunks with `diff -u --label a/<file> --label b/<file>` (new files
# from /dev/null), and update the hashes in cmake/hactool.cmake.
